{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":1,"query":"name=Paglen&limit=10&title=How to See Like a Machine","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":{"title":"How to see like a machine ","subTitle":"images after AI "},"name":{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Paglen, Trevor","role":[{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"code","@authority":"marcrelator","#text":"aut"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"code","@authority":"marcrelator","#text":"http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/relators/aut"}}],"nameIdentifier":["https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJht6FD94jJMqBtRDXPCwC","http://id.loc.gov/rwo/agents/no2006112502"]},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","@valueURI":"http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/contentTypes/txt","#text":"text"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Essays"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Informational works"},{"@authority":"lcgft","#text":"Informational works"},{"@authority":"lcgft","#text":"Essays"},{"@authority":"rvmgf","#text":"Documents d'information."}],"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"enk"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"England"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2026"},"copyrightDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2026"},"issuance":"monographic"},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"London :"}},"agent":{"namePart":"Verso,","role":{"roleTerm":"publisher"}},"dateIssued":"2026.","issuance":"single unit"}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":[{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},{"@authority":"marccategory","#text":"text"},{"@authority":"marcsmd","#text":"regular print"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"unmediated"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"volume"}],"extent":"176 pages : illustrations ; 22 cm"},{"form":{"@type":"Illustrative content","#text":"illustration"}}],"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"\"Today our world is under the watchful and tireless eye of computer vision, with cam­eras and monitors tracing our every move. Furthermore, generative AI is now able to render a synthetic world indistinguishable from reality for us to explore. Trevor Paglen goes in search of the ways and means of understanding this new visual universe. Instead of asking what these technologies \"say\" about the world, he teaches us to ask what they \"do\" and where such images come from. Exploring the esoteric worlds of psyops, UFO imagery, magicians, and public relation gurus, Paglen shows that this appar­ently alien realm is more human, but much stranger, than we imagine\"-- Book jacket."},"tableOfContents":{"@type":"Contents","#text":"Introduction -- Invisible images (your pictures are looking at you) -- Machine realism : this is an apple -- Machine realism : this is not an apple -- Neural activations : how tortured kittens, the face of Jesus on a slice of toast, and nacho cheese Doritos help explain generative AI -- Society of the psyop. Part I: UFOs and the future of media ; Part II: AI, mind control, and magic ; Part III: Cognition and chaos -- The archives of the future : thoughts on generative media and theology -- Conclusion."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Trevor Paglen."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references (pages 155-165) and index."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Image (Philosophy)"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Generative artificial intelligence","Social aspects"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Books"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Image (Philosophie)"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Travail"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Livres"},{"@authority":"aat","topic":"labo